21, Stage D: RESTORED BY HAND after the retirement check retired it.  The item was re-certified because its svgRead coordinates moved (the per-character width table re-laid-out the drawing, and the ruler row now sits at y=320);  its stem, choices, key, passage and dataTable are unchanged.  That run returned agree, and the retirement check re-asked twice more and got agree both times, three of three, so it retired the adjudication.  Across both sessions the item now reads 4 agree against 3 disagree over seven runs on text the blind pass cannot tell apart, which is an unstable item, not a settled one;  a result that discards a human decision needs more than the latest three draws when the earlier three went the other way.  The key stands on the drawing, as above.",
